<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Torf-Einarr</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. c. 900</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a> · Also known as Turf-Einar</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Torf-Einarr was an Earl of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/orkney">Orkney</a> around 900, a son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rognvald-eysteinsson">Rognvald Eysteinsson</a> of Møre according to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/orkneyinga-saga">Orkneyinga saga</a>. He won the islands from Danish raiders, and the saga says he got his name from teaching the islanders to cut peat, or turf, for fuel. He killed Halfdan, a son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harald-fairhair">Harald Fairhair</a>, and his descendants ruled Orkney for centuries.</p></div>
